This document provides the complete technical implementation for the Case Transfer AI Summarization feature. It supersedes all previous versions and addresses all outstanding feedback.

---

1. Solution Overview

The Case Transfer AI Summarization feature is designed to improve the efficiency and quality of case handoffs between support agents. When a Case is transferred from one agent to another, the new owner often spends considerable time reading through the entire case history (emails, comments, description) to get up to speed. This process is time-consuming and can lead to inconsistent understanding of the case status.

This solution automates the creation of a concise summary upon case owner change. It leverages an external Large Language Model (LLM) to analyze the case history and generate a summary. This summary is then stored in a custom object and displayed prominently on the Case record page, providing the new owner with an immediate, high-quality overview of the case.

The core process is as follows:
1.  An agent changes the OwnerId of a Case record to another user.
2.  An after update trigger on the Case object fires.
3.  The trigger invokes a handler class, which identifies the relevant cases and enqueues an asynchronous Apex Queueable job.
4.  The Queueable job orchestrates the summarization process to avoid hitting governor limits and blocking the user interface.
5.  A service class gathers relevant data from the Case (e.g., Description, recent Case Comments, Email Messages) and constructs a prompt for the LLM.
6.  A dedicated callout service sends the prompt to the external LLM API and receives the generated summary.
7.  The summary is saved in a new Case_Transfer_Summary__c record, linked to the parent Case.
8.  A Lightning Web Component (LWC) on the Case Lightning Record Page displays the most recent summary.

This asynchronous, service-oriented architecture ensures the solution is scalable, maintainable, and does not negatively impact the user experience during the case transfer process.

